      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The historic Sydenstricker Schoolhouse, built in 1928 near West Springfield, was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 2012.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Springfield%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Springfield’s Richard Byrd Library, opened in 1965 and expanded to 15,000 square feet in 2010, honors famed aviator Richard E. Byrd.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Springfield%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Springfield Interchange, where I‑95, I‑395, and the Capital Beltway meet, dominates the town’s geography.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Springfield%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Franconia–Springfield Metro station, a key transit hub, connects Springfield to downtown Washington, Arlington, and the Pentagon.",
